52a53,68
> - Always compare the two windows: for each difference, state what the behaviour looked
>   like in the earlier window as well as in the later one.
> - REL items show how two activities relate in each window. Activities that rarely or
>   never occur in the same trace in one window but usually do in the other changed between
>   being alternatives and being executed together.
> - Activities that appear in both orders in similar proportions are executed without a
>   fixed order between them. A change between a fixed order and such a mixed order is a
>   change in ordering constraints, not an exchange of positions.
> - A change in how often existing paths are taken requires that every activity and path
>   involved is observed in a substantial share of traces in both windows, and that only the
>   shares between alternatives shift; it is not a replacement of one path by another.
>   It does not apply when an activity or path is (nearly) absent in one window, when a
>   predecessor now leads directly to a successor so that a group of activities is
>   bypassed, or when the number of repetitions per trace changes: these indicate that
>   activities were added or removed, became optional or mandatory, or became repeated or
>   stopped repeating.
